  "full_response": "Here’s a structured **training slide deck outline** for **\"Protecting CLASSIFIED_DATA and CONFIDENTIAL Materials in the Workplace\"**. This outline balances policy, practical guidance, and engagement to ensure comprehension and retention.\n\n---\n\n### **Slide Deck Title:**\n**\"Safeguarding CLASSIFIED_DATA & CONFIDENTIAL Information: Your Role in Security\"**\n*Subtitle:* *\"A Practical Guide for Employees\"*\n\n---\n\n### **Slide Deck Outline**\n\n#### **1. Title Slide**\n- Title + subtitle\n- Presenter name/department\n- Date\n- Organization logo\n\n#### **2. Introduction & Objectives**\n- **Purpose:** Why this training matters (e.g., legal compliance, national security, corporate integrity).\n- **Learning Objectives:**\n  1. Define CLASSIFIED_DATA and CONFIDENTIAL information.\n  2. Identify risks and consequences of mishandling.\n  3. Apply best practices for storage, transmission, and disposal.\n  4. Recognize and report security incidents.\n- **Agenda:** Overview of topics covered.\n\n#### **3. Understanding the Basics**\n- **Definitions:**\n  - *CLASSIFIED_DATA*: Government/military classifications (e.g., Top Secret, Secret, Confidential).\n  - *CONFIDENTIAL Information*: Corporate/proprietary data (e.g., trade secrets, PII, financial records).\n- **Key Differences:** Classification levels vs. corporate confidentiality tiers.\n- **Examples:** Real-world scenarios (e.g., leaked documents, phishing attacks).\n\n#### **4. Legal & Regulatory Framework**\n- **Applicable Laws/Policies:**\n  - Government: Executive Order 13526 (U.S.), Official Secrets Act (UK), etc.\n  - Corporate: GDPR, HIPAA, NIST, ISO 27001, company-specific policies.\n- **Penalties for Non-Compliance:**\n  - Fines, termination, criminal charges (e.g., Espionage Act).\n  - Case studies (e.g., Snowden, corporate breaches).\n\n#### **5. Risks & Threats**\n- **Common Threats:**\n  - Cyber: Phishing, malware, insider threats.\n  - Physical: Unattended documents, tailgating, improper disposal.\n  - Human Error: Misaddressed emails, lost devices, oversharing.\n- **Consequences:**\n  - Data breaches, reput",
